WEBVTT

00:00:00.321 --> 00:00:02.790
Here's the cosine curve, with x in radians.

00:00:03.493 --> 00:00:04.278
Let's give it a meaning.

00:00:04.902 --> 00:00:06.802
It's the swell at a marker buoy off

00:00:06.843 --> 00:00:07.422
a surf beach:

00:00:08.083 --> 00:00:10.063
x is the time in seconds, which this

00:00:10.124 --> 00:00:12.464
model also uses as the angle in radians,

00:00:12.906 --> 00:00:13.845
one radian per second,

00:00:14.426 --> 00:00:16.666
and y is the buoy's height in metres

00:00:16.867 --> 00:00:17.847
above calm water.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.758
Now change the equation to y equals two

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:24.828
cos of x minus pi over three, plus

00:00:24.909 --> 00:00:25.009
one.

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.876
That's a second buoy further along the beach,

00:00:28.358 --> 00:00:30.001
on a day with bigger swell and a

00:00:30.042 --> 00:00:30.662
higher tide.

00:00:31.326 --> 00:00:34.203
The curve gets taller, lifts up and slides.

00:00:34.809 --> 00:00:35.641
But look at the peak.

00:00:36.127 --> 00:00:38.776
The bracket says minus pi over three, yet

00:00:38.837 --> 00:00:41.024
the peak has moved right, to pi over

00:00:41.046 --> 00:00:41.285
three.

00:00:42.029 --> 00:00:43.816
Each part of the equation does one job.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:45.395
Let's take them one at a time.

00:00:46.009 --> 00:00:47.356
Start outside the bracket.

00:00:48.059 --> 00:00:50.102
In y equals two cos x,

00:00:50.604 --> 00:00:52.606
every height is multiplied by two:

00:00:53.228 --> 00:00:54.550
a swell twice as big.

00:00:55.212 --> 00:00:57.672
Peaks at one rise to two, troughs fall

00:00:57.693 --> 00:00:59.514
to minus two, and the points on the

00:00:59.675 --> 00:01:02.595
axis stay put, because two times zero is

00:01:02.636 --> 00:01:03.216
still zero.

00:01:04.038 --> 00:01:06.331
This is a vertical dilation by a factor

00:01:06.352 --> 00:01:06.714
of two.

00:01:07.459 --> 00:01:09.984
The amplitude, the distance from the middle line

00:01:10.086 --> 00:01:11.388
up to a peak, is now two.

00:01:12.512 --> 00:01:14.099
What if the factor is minus two?

00:01:14.863 --> 00:01:17.129
Every height changes sign, so the curve flips

00:01:17.271 --> 00:01:18.072
over the x-axis.

00:01:18.755 --> 00:01:20.942
The amplitude is still two, because a distance

00:01:21.003 --> 00:01:21.685
can't be negative.

00:01:22.375 --> 00:01:24.603
Now add one, outside the bracket.

00:01:25.086 --> 00:01:26.368
That's the tide coming in:

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:29.294
every height goes up by one, so the

00:01:29.315 --> 00:01:31.478
whole curve slides up one unit.

00:01:32.101 --> 00:01:34.610
Its middle line, the midline, moves from the

00:01:34.792 --> 00:01:36.438
x-axis to y equals one.

00:01:37.745 --> 00:01:40.058
The shape doesn't change, so the amplitude is

00:01:40.099 --> 00:01:40.782
still two.

00:01:41.507 --> 00:01:43.728
The highest value is the midline plus the

00:01:43.789 --> 00:01:46.369
amplitude, three, and the lowest is the midline

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:48.351
minus the amplitude, minus one.

00:01:48.913 --> 00:01:50.747
So the range is from minus one to

00:01:50.809 --> 00:01:51.050
three.

00:01:51.736 --> 00:01:52.963
Now the surprising one,

00:01:53.568 --> 00:01:54.352
inside the bracket.

00:01:54.956 --> 00:01:56.860
The second buoy is further along the beach,

00:01:57.222 --> 00:01:59.306
so each wave reaches it a little later.

00:02:00.008 --> 00:02:01.892
Its height now is what the first buoy's

00:02:01.933 --> 00:02:04.439
height was pi over three seconds ago.

00:02:05.042 --> 00:02:07.578
That's cos of x minus pi over three.

00:02:08.304 --> 00:02:10.069
The first buoy peaked where the inside was

00:02:10.131 --> 00:02:10.511
zero.

00:02:11.075 --> 00:02:13.107
Now the inside is zero when x equals

00:02:13.168 --> 00:02:13.872
pi over three.

00:02:14.617 --> 00:02:16.865
Everything happens pi over three later,

00:02:17.368 --> 00:02:19.536
so the graph slides right by pi over

00:02:19.597 --> 00:02:19.877
three.

00:02:20.541 --> 00:02:22.107
That's a horizontal translation.

00:02:22.791 --> 00:02:25.127
The minus sign means later, a slide to

00:02:25.149 --> 00:02:25.510
the right.

00:02:26.035 --> 00:02:28.308
A plus sign would mean earlier, a slide

00:02:28.349 --> 00:02:28.811
to the left.

00:02:29.442 --> 00:02:31.178
What about a number multiplying x?

00:02:32.003 --> 00:02:34.632
A choppy swell brings waves twice as often.

00:02:35.274 --> 00:02:38.220
In y equals cos two x, the inside

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.064
runs twice as fast as x.

00:02:40.866 --> 00:02:43.154
One full cycle needs the inside to go

00:02:43.214 --> 00:02:45.662
from zero to two pi, and that's finished

00:02:45.923 --> 00:02:47.067
when x reaches pi.

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:49.814
So the period, the time for one cycle,

00:02:50.215 --> 00:02:52.600
halves to pi, about three seconds.

00:02:53.322 --> 00:02:56.167
The graph is squashed towards the y-axis, a

00:02:56.228 --> 00:02:58.813
horizontal dilation by a factor of one half.

00:02:59.897 --> 00:03:02.526
For sine and cosine with positive a, the

00:03:02.568 --> 00:03:04.916
period is two pi divided by a.

00:03:05.599 --> 00:03:07.667
A half inside would double the period to

00:03:07.748 --> 00:03:10.198
four pi, a long, slow groundswell.

00:03:10.855 --> 00:03:13.464
When there's a number multiplying x and a

00:03:13.545 --> 00:03:14.387
number added,

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:16.475
take the number out first.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:20.235
Here's y equals sine of two x plus

00:03:20.296 --> 00:03:20.597
pi.

00:03:21.363 --> 00:03:23.413
It's tempting to say it slides left by

00:03:23.475 --> 00:03:23.735
pi.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:26.964
But the inside is zero when two x

00:03:27.025 --> 00:03:28.206
plus pi is zero,

00:03:28.809 --> 00:03:31.032
which is at x equals minus pi over

00:03:31.053 --> 00:03:31.232
two.

00:03:32.255 --> 00:03:34.459
Factor out the two, and you get sine

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.406
of two, bracket x plus pi over two.

00:03:38.108 --> 00:03:40.051
So, squash by a factor of a half,

00:03:40.554 --> 00:03:42.978
then slide left by pi over two.

00:03:43.821 --> 00:03:46.404
Sliding left by pi would land right back

00:03:46.545 --> 00:03:49.349
on sine two x, which is wrong: the

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:51.713
true curve is upside down compared with it.

00:03:52.429 --> 00:03:54.901
The same rules work for tan x, with

00:03:55.103 --> 00:03:55.685
two differences.

00:03:56.409 --> 00:03:58.869
Tan x repeats every pi, not two pi,

00:03:59.251 --> 00:04:01.891
so in y equals tan two x, the

00:04:01.932 --> 00:04:03.752
period is pi divided by two,

00:04:04.293 --> 00:04:04.913
pi over two.

00:04:05.894 --> 00:04:08.638
The asymptotes, the vertical lines the curve never

00:04:08.699 --> 00:04:11.583
meets, move with the squash, to pi over

00:04:11.644 --> 00:04:13.887
four, three pi over four, and so on,

00:04:14.289 --> 00:04:15.069
every pi over two.

00:04:15.934 --> 00:04:18.648
And tan has no highest or lowest value.

00:04:19.312 --> 00:04:21.337
Its range is all real numbers, so it

00:04:21.379 --> 00:04:22.401
has no amplitude.

00:04:23.164 --> 00:04:25.232
A number in front still stretches it vertically,

00:04:25.373 --> 00:04:27.782
by that dilation factor, but it's not called

00:04:27.823 --> 00:04:28.364
an amplitude.

00:04:29.076 --> 00:04:29.802
Let's put it together.

00:04:30.565 --> 00:04:33.847
For y equals minus three cos of two

00:04:33.968 --> 00:04:37.111
x minus pi over two, minus one, describe

00:04:37.132 --> 00:04:41.436
the transformations, and state the amplitude, period, horizontal

00:04:41.477 --> 00:04:43.017
translation and range.

00:04:44.241 --> 00:04:45.705
Factor the inside first:

00:04:46.429 --> 00:04:47.511
two, bracket

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:49.578
x minus pi over four.

00:04:50.362 --> 00:04:50.522
So,

00:04:51.025 --> 00:04:53.193
squash horizontally by a factor of a half:

00:04:53.676 --> 00:04:54.719
the period is pi.

00:04:55.484 --> 00:04:57.350
Slide right by pi over four.

00:04:57.993 --> 00:05:00.518
Stretch vertically by a factor of three and

00:05:00.559 --> 00:05:03.664
reflect in the x-axis: the amplitude is three.

00:05:04.427 --> 00:05:07.398
Then shift down one, so the midline is

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:09.024
y equals minus one.

00:05:09.828 --> 00:05:12.216
The range runs from minus four to two.

00:05:13.339 --> 00:05:16.143
To sketch it, mark one cycle from pi

00:05:16.164 --> 00:05:18.667
over four to five pi over four, with

00:05:18.688 --> 00:05:20.290
a key point every quarter period.

00:05:21.173 --> 00:05:23.458
At pi over four, the inside is zero,

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:26.566
cos is one, and y is minus four:

00:05:27.128 --> 00:05:28.872
a trough, as the reflection predicts.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:30.921
Try this on a graphing app:

00:05:31.562 --> 00:05:33.983
build the curve one change at a time,

00:05:34.404 --> 00:05:36.885
and each step lands exactly where the rules

00:05:36.945 --> 00:05:37.146
say.

00:05:37.988 --> 00:05:38.875
Here's a way to remember it.

00:05:39.578 --> 00:05:42.044
Outside the bracket changes y, and does what

00:05:42.084 --> 00:05:42.405
it says:

00:05:43.026 --> 00:05:45.151
times minus three, then minus one.

00:05:45.972 --> 00:05:47.213
Inside the bracket changes x,

00:05:48.114 --> 00:05:48.955
and does the opposite:

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:51.177
times two squashes by a half,

00:05:51.737 --> 00:05:54.219
and, once you've factored, minus pi over four

00:05:54.399 --> 00:05:55.060
slides right.

00:05:57.770 --> 00:05:58.173
Your turn.

00:05:58.899 --> 00:06:00.902
A buoy's height above the sea floor, in

00:06:00.943 --> 00:06:02.345
metres, after x seconds,

00:06:02.907 --> 00:06:05.872
is y equals minus two cos of three

00:06:06.014 --> 00:06:08.057
x minus pi over two, plus four.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:12.290
State the amplitude, the period, the horizontal translation,

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:13.233
and the range.

00:06:13.877 --> 00:06:14.783
Pause here to answer.

00:06:25.377 --> 00:06:26.669
The amplitude is two.

00:06:27.276 --> 00:06:29.311
The period is two pi over three.

00:06:30.178 --> 00:06:31.160
Factor the inside:

00:06:31.722 --> 00:06:34.609
three, bracket x minus pi over six, so

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:36.473
it slides right by pi over six.

00:06:37.217 --> 00:06:39.347
The midline is four, so the range is

00:06:39.389 --> 00:06:40.674
from two to six metres.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:43.928
Sliding right by pi over two forgets to

00:06:43.969 --> 00:06:44.872
factor out the three.

00:06:46.598 --> 00:06:47.022
Last one.

00:06:47.746 --> 00:06:50.729
Describe the transformations that map y equals tan

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:51.690
x onto y

00:06:52.232 --> 00:06:55.035
equals tan of x over two, plus one.

00:06:55.617 --> 00:06:57.789
Then state the period and the range.

00:06:58.478 --> 00:06:59.328
Pause here to answer.

00:07:10.128 --> 00:07:12.752
Inside, x over two does the opposite of

00:07:12.874 --> 00:07:15.859
halving: it's a horizontal dilation by a factor

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:16.280
of two.

00:07:17.104 --> 00:07:19.802
Outside, plus one shifts the graph up one

00:07:19.923 --> 00:07:20.104
unit.

00:07:20.827 --> 00:07:23.353
Tan repeats every pi, so the period is

00:07:23.434 --> 00:07:26.039
pi divided by a half: two pi.

00:07:26.663 --> 00:07:28.109
The range is all real numbers.

00:07:28.733 --> 00:07:30.758
Four pi comes from using the sine and

00:07:30.819 --> 00:07:33.165
cos rule, two pi over a, for tan.

00:07:34.728 --> 00:07:37.813
So outside changes the heights as written, and

00:07:38.014 --> 00:07:40.859
inside changes the x values the opposite way.

00:07:41.824 --> 00:07:44.281
Next, we'll use these graphs to solve equations.

00:07:45.206 --> 00:07:47.088
Here's a city's daylight over one year:

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:50.655
twelve plus two sine of x minus pi

00:07:50.696 --> 00:07:53.020
over six hours, where the whole year is

00:07:53.101 --> 00:07:53.581
two pi.

00:07:54.442 --> 00:07:57.063
On which days is there exactly thirteen hours

00:07:57.104 --> 00:07:59.005
of daylight, and how can we be sure

00:07:59.046 --> 00:08:00.046
we've found every one?

00:08:02.788 --> 00:08:03.671
Here are the key notes.

00:08:04.194 --> 00:08:05.962
Pause the video if you need more time

00:08:05.983 --> 00:08:06.464
to copy them.
